<h1><span lang="EN-GB">New Cylinder</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-US">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Datuming &gt; Cylinder</b></span><span class="Path">,</span> by using the shortcut <span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Shift + Alt + 5</b></span> <span class="Shortcut">or by choosing the</span> <span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Cylinder</b></span> <span class="Shortcut">tab in the</span> <span class="Shortcut" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Datum creation</u></span> <span class="Shortcut">mode (if it is currently active).</span></p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> New Cylinder command creates new datum cylinder by one of the 2 available methods. Here below these methods are explained followed by examples.</p>
<h2 class="whs4"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">Methods:</span></i></h2>
<p class="sub-head"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">Interactive</span></i></p>
<p><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="../images/new_cylinder_interactive.gif" width="33px" height="30px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></span></i> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">: standard cylinder construction using one of the available 4</span></i> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">definition</span></i> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">methods (pick from viewport is enabled by default). For more details about the define section, see <a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_cylinder.htm">Define Cylinder</a>.</span></i></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-style:normal; text-decoration:underline;"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></i></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP238104921" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/InteractiveCylinder.gif" width="534px" height="550px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="whs7">Changes of all values can be applied at any time. Flip the axis direction of the final datum using the "<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>+/-</b></span>" button in the result section, if necessary.</p>
<p class="sub-head">By circle and axis length</p>
<p><img src="../images/new_cylinder_by_circle.gif" width="32px" height="29px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""> : This method includes definition of a construction circle and 2 parameters: for axis length and for direction.</p>
<p id="P1"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>How it works</b></i></span>:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered-IP1">
<p id="P1" class="Numbered">The user defines a circle. For more details about circle definition, see <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_circle.htm">Define Circle</a>.</span></i></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered-IP1">
<p id="P1" class="Numbered"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">T</span></i>hen cylinder length should be set.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CNumbered-IP1">
<p id="P1" class="Numbered">Cylinder direction should be chosen. There are 3 possibilities for cylinder direction/position:</p>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-IP1">
<p id="P1" class="bullet">the constructed circle is set as cylinder basis and cylinder axis is identical to the circle normal, this is the default option.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-IP1">
<p id="P1" class="bullet">the constructed circle is set as cylinder basis and cylinder axis is opposite to the circle normal</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-IP1">
<p id="P1" class="bullet">the constructed circle is set in the middle of cylinder length and cylinder axis is identical to the circle normal</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="P1">Changes of all values can be applied at any time. Flip the axis direction of the final datum using the "<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>+/-</b></span>" button in the result section, if necessary.</p>
<p id="P1" class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP936692118" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
